{"id": "3f7ac4e5-2ad4-475d-8996-6f21bb604a97", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I notice AWS-DisableS3BucketPublicReadWrite only sets RestrictPublicBuckets and IgnorePublicAcls, leaving BlockPublicAcls and BlockPublicPolicy unset—and since PutPublicAccessBlock overwrites the entire existing config with omitted fields defaulting to false, this could actually weaken pre-existing protections. That's worth flagging, along with checking AWSConfigRemediation-ConfigureS3BucketPublicAccessBlock for the same issue.

Actually, that remediation sets all four settings to true by default and requires an AutomationAssumeRole, so I'll recommend it instead—classifying it as mutating-reversible per the catalog. Time to write up the answer.

"}]}
